mvn package going to download lots of dependencies, docker image building procelss is going to take lot of time
writing docker file in two stages 

stage 1:
F baseimage
W /app
R dependencies
R jar

stage 2:
F baseimage
W /app
C buildstage/*.jar .
E 
CMD java -jar 

building of application is done in one stage like genertation of jar file in second stage we are going to copy the jar file only excluding the dependencies and source code, so final docker image will be the size of stage 2.

# ===== Build Stage =====
FROM maven:3.9.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
WORKDIR /app

# Copy pom.xml first to leverage Docker layer caching
COPY pom.xml .

# Pre-download dependencies (faster rebuilds)
RUN mvn -B -q -DskipTests dependency:go-offline     >> -B means there will be no promt comming  and dependencies are going to download offline

# Copy project source
COPY src ./src    >> copying the application soucre code

# Build the JAR (skip tests for faster build)
RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests  >> skipping the test cases and building the application jar file /app/target/*.jar file

# ===== Runtime Stage =====
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine   >> taking the base image which contains the jdk only as maven not required now  this base image will be small in size
WORKDIR /app

# Copy built jar from build stage
COPY --from=build /app/target/*.jar app.jar  >> copying something from the previuos stage 

# Expose app port
EXPOSE 8080

# Run the app
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"] 

